# ------------------------------------------------------------- paper source
# The paper being reproduced is not redistributed from this repository. Both the
# PDF and its extracted text are kept locally and deliberately untracked; nothing
# under cccplus/, experiments/ or tests/ reads either of them.
Cycle_Consistent_Translation_for_Cross_Model_Mechanism_Comparison.pdf
paper.txt
*.pdf

# ================================================================= artifacts
# Two rules, for two different reasons.

# 1. Caches: ~1 GB of torch tensors. Regenerable — the translator cache is refit by
#    run_controlled.py (about 26 min cold), the SIIT checkpoints by
#    train_controlled.py (about 59 min, and resumable). Never commit these: a
#    silently-rewritten translator cache has already produced inconsistent numbers
#    once in this project's history, and versioning it would hide that rather than
#    surface it.
results/cache/

# 2. Per-path measurement dumps: ~18.6 MB of the ~19.6 MB of JSON in results/, and
#    rewritten in full on every run. Committing them would add ~19 MB to history per
#    regeneration. They are raw intermediates: every reported number is derived from
#    them into results/*analysis*.json, which IS tracked. To share them for
#    re-analysis without re-running, attach them to a release rather than a commit.
results/*_paths*.json

# Hugging Face / datasets caches, if anyone points them at the tree
.cache/
huggingface/

# ================================================================= kept on purpose
# Tracked, because these are the results and their provenance:
#   results/controlled_analysis*.json        per-rule metrics, contrasts, bounds
#   results/controlled_benchmark_models.json the SIIT gate and the retry ladder
#   results/multisite_results.json           Sec. 3.7 extension
#   results/natural_*_tiny.json              self-test output; see the README warning
#   results/tables/                          the emitted Markdown and LaTeX tables
#   manifest/manifest.yaml                   the frozen config every result is hashed to
